    <label>Watcher long-range precision turret</label>
    <description>The Watcher is an experimental smart-projectile turret at the edge of current weapons technology, built to engage distant, high-value, and high-threat targets. After a brief analysis cycle, it fires three high-precision smart rounds in rapid succession, delivering a fast and concentrated pinpoint strike. Even moving targets or enemies relying on cover struggle to fully escape its ballistic correction. The tradeoff is just as clear: its specialized ammunition is expensive, and the complex guidance mechanisms require advanced components for upkeep, so the Watcher is poorly suited to wasting firepower on ordinary enemies.\n\nProcurement once asked why every shot had to be a three-round burst.\nThe engineer replied, "The first confirms the prediction, the second corrects the error, and the third makes sure the first two do not look wasted."\nAfter that, procurement requested that all ammunition unit costs be removed from the report.</description>
